> So does this mean the perception widely reported
> that holding XL to 14 makes the whole game, but
> especially the Planes, easier, is completely wrong?
> Never having been to the planes, I don't know from
> my own experience.

It will make the general run of random monsters easier than they would
otherwise have been down to level 43 or so (the effect being more
noticeable the shallower you are); since that takes you at least
halfway through Gehennom, it may still be considered worthwhile.  It
will also have an effect on the Planes in extending the lower bound of
eligible monsters, as I mentioned; nothing hugely significant, but
it's there.

The greater effect is going to be on the _non_-random monsters, the
preplaced ones that aren't specified exactly but are "any L" or the
like. There's a direct "skew towards lower value monsters at lower
exp. levels" in the code that chooses these.

